<title>FRANCE: Bouygues rises on merger plans.</title>
<headline>Bouygues rises on merger plans.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French construction firm Bouygues rose on Friday, following news of its plans to take over and merge three subsidiaries, in a move which will strengthen its balance sheet.</p>
<p>The stock was up 2.15 percent at 523 francs at 0955 GMT, on volume of 45,847 shares. The market was up 0.79 percent.</p>
<p>Bouygues has called an extraordinary shareholders meeting for November 26 to approve a plan to take over and merge its CFTR, Minoterie Parisienne and Fremoulin units, which will boost the group's asset value by 1.36 billion francs.</p>
</text>
